    <summary>GitHub Desktop Beta: the latest features and bug fixes being tested for the next production release.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[**DISCLAIMER: This package provides the "Beta" builds of GitHub Desktop. It differs from the standard `github-desktop` package by installing the beta release channel. Use this if you want to test new features before they hit the stable channel.**

Focus on what matters instead of fighting with Git. Whether you're new to Git or a seasoned user, GitHub Desktop simplifies your development workflow.

## Features

- **Attribute commits with collaborators easily**: quickly add co-authors to your commit. See the attribution on the history page, undo an accidental attribution, and see the co-authors on github.com.
- **Check out branches with pull requests and view CI statuses**: see all open pull requests for your repositories and check them out as if they were a local branch, even if they're from upstream branches or forks.
- **Syntax highlighted diffs**: syntax highlighting when viewing diffs for a variety of languages.
- **Expanded image diff support**: see the before and after, swipe or fade between the two, or look at just the changed parts.
- **Extensive editor and shell integrations**: open your favorite editor or shell from the app, or jump back to GitHub Desktop from your shell.
- **Community supported**: GitHub Desktop is open source. Check out the roadmap, contribute, and help make collaboration even easier.

## Notes

- 64-bit Windows only. The application is installed for the user running the installation (per-user install).
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://desktop.github.com/release-notes/?env=beta</releaseNotes>
